<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Frontend Development on Winner's Dev Notes</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/categories/frontend-development/</link><description>Recent content in Frontend Development on Winner's Dev Notes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://releaseleaf.com/categories/frontend-development/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Limit JavaScript Async Batches with a Worker Pool</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/jsasynclimit.html</link><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/jsasynclimit.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Loading a list of JSON files with &lt;code&gt;Promise.all(urls.map(loadJson))&lt;/code&gt; is convenient, but the mapping step calls &lt;code&gt;loadJson&lt;/code&gt; for every URL immediately. For a large batch, that can create more outstanding work than the application needs.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A small worker pool lets you choose how many operations may be in flight. This example works with promise-based JavaScript functions in a browser or Node.js. It is useful for application-managed downloads and tooling; engine asset loaders may already have their own scheduling rules.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Prevent Stale Fetch Results with AbortController and Request IDs</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/fetchstale.html</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/fetchstale.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A search box can display the wrong results even when every HTTP request succeeds. A player types &lt;code&gt;sword&lt;/code&gt;, then changes the query to &lt;code&gt;shield&lt;/code&gt;. If the first request finishes last, an unguarded callback replaces the shield results with swords.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Use an &lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt; to cancel obsolete network work and a request ID to decide which result may update the interface. This example targets browser pages, including Cocos Creator Web builds with the required browser APIs. Check API support separately before adapting it to a native game runtime.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Safari Remote Debugging for iPhone: Web Inspector and Develop Menu</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/saredeipwe.html</link><pubDate>Wed, 11 Feb 2026 16:49:17 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/saredeipwe.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A previous article covered &#13;&#10;&lt;a href="https://lengmo714.top/343880cb.html" title="debugging a mobile web page with Chrome" rel="noopener external nofollow noreferrer" target="_blank" class=" exturl"&gt;&#13;&#10; debugging a mobile web page with Chrome&#13;&#10; &#13;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;. This guide explains how to debug a page open in Safari on an iPhone.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="remote-debugging-requirements"&gt;Remote Debugging Requirements&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#remote-debugging-requirements"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;You need both a Mac and an iPhone. This workflow is not available from a Windows computer.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="inspect-an-iphone-safari-tab-from-a-mac"&gt;Inspect an iPhone Safari Tab from a Mac&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#inspect-an-iphone-safari-tab-from-a-mac"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Enable &lt;strong&gt;Web Inspector&lt;/strong&gt; on the iPhone. Open &lt;strong&gt;Settings → Apps → Safari → Advanced&lt;/strong&gt;, then turn on Web Inspector.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;img src="https://releaseleaf.com/postImg/1369ddb7/1.png" alt="Enable Web Inspector" decoding="async" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open Safari on the Mac and use the Develop menu as shown below:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;img src="https://releaseleaf.com/postImg/1369ddb7/2.png" alt="Open the Develop menu" decoding="async" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The target page must also be open in Safari on the iPhone; otherwise it will not appear in the Mac&amp;rsquo;s Develop menu.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Select the web page you want to inspect. Safari opens its developer tools:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;img src="https://releaseleaf.com/postImg/1369ddb7/3.png" alt="Safari developer tools" decoding="async" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;</description></item><item><title>Detect iOS and iPadOS in Frontend Code: User Agent, MacIntel and Touch</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/deioipfrco.html</link><pubDate>Thu, 06 Nov 2025 10:53:08 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/deioipfrco.html</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Frontend projects sometimes need to identify the device type—for example, whether the visitor is using iOS or Android.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="why-user-agent-checks-miss-ipados"&gt;Why User-Agent Checks Miss iPadOS&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#why-user-agent-checks-miss-ipados"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Traditionally, an iOS check might inspect only the browser&amp;rsquo;s user agent:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/iPhone|iPad|iPod/i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;navigator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userAgent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This does not reliably identify newer iPads. Starting with iPadOS 13, an iPad can report its platform as &lt;code&gt;MacIntel&lt;/code&gt;, causing it to be mistaken for a Mac.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Use a combined check instead:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-1"&gt; 1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-2"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-2"&gt; 2&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-3"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-3"&gt; 3&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-4"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-4"&gt; 4&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-5"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-5"&gt; 5&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-6"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-6"&gt; 6&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-7"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-7"&gt; 7&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-8"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-8"&gt; 8&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-9"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-9"&gt; 9&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-10"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-10"&gt;10&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ts" data-lang="ts"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getDeviceType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Android&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;iOS&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;unknown&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ua&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;navigator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userAgent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;navigator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;vendor&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;opera&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;platform&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;navigator&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;platform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxTouchPoints&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;navigator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxTouchPoints&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/Android/i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ua&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Android&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/iPad|iPhone|iPod/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ua&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;iOS&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;platform&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;MacIntel&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxTouchPoints&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;iOS&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;unknown&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Although iPadOS 13 and later can identify the device as &lt;code&gt;MacIntel&lt;/code&gt;, an iPad still supports multitouch. Checking &lt;code&gt;navigator.maxTouchPoints &amp;gt; 1&lt;/code&gt; distinguishes it from a typical Mac.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Chrome Remote Debugging for Android: USB and chrome://inspect</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/chredeanus.html</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 May 2024 20:00:13 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/chredeanus.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Install Chrome on the PC and Android phone and connect them with a data cable.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Enable Developer options and USB debugging on the phone.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In desktop Chrome, open Extensions → Manage Extensions and enable Developer mode.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://pic.imgdb.cn/item/66586a1dd9c307b7e993fcc5.png" alt="Developer mode"&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;chrome://inspect/#devices&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Connect the phone, approve USB debugging and file-access prompts, then refresh the page.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://pic.imgdb.cn/item/66586a21d9c307b7e99411a9.png" alt="Remote devices"&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open the target page in mobile Chrome and click &lt;code&gt;inspect&lt;/code&gt; beside it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If &lt;code&gt;Remote Target&lt;/code&gt; is missing, verify the cable, USB mode, drivers, and debugging authorization. Each open mobile tab appears as a separate inspectable entry.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>